WEBVTT

00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:03.710
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.670
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.730
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.470
<b>Kinou made no ruuru kyou wa tada no ruuzu</b>

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:20.470
<i>Yesterday’s rules are simply loose today</i>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.770
<b>Kowashite dantotsu gooru</b>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.770
<i>The best goal is to break them</i>

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.560
<b>hashiri tudukete nai to</b>

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:27.560
<i>If I don’t keep running</i>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.900
<b>hokani imi wa nai to</b>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.900
<i>There’s no other meaning</i>

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.240
<b>Panku na tetsukaku nanda</b>

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.240
<i>It’s a punk philosophy</i>

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:39.330
<b>Baiorizumu wa tsuubai rizumu de</b>

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:39.330
<i>Biorhythm is a two-time rhythm</i>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.460
<b>Fuukei wa shunkan ni musuu no sen</b>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.460
<i>The scenery instantly becomes countless lines</i>

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.330
<b>Ore wo torimaku kaze</b>

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:46.330
<i>The wind envelops me</i>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<b>Inside Outside semete</b>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<i>Inside Outside attack</i>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<b>Issai gassai nuite</b>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<i>Surpass everything altogether</i>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.570
<b>Dare hitori monani hitotsu mo</b>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.050
<i>I won’t let no one and nothing go forward</i>

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:58.050
<b>Mae wo ikasetaku wa nai</b>

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.430
<b>Inside Outside GO! SONIC!!</b>

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.430
<i>Inside Outside, Go! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<b>Issai gassai Yes! SONIC!!</b>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<i>Everything altogether Yes! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.890
<b>Abunai yo to Have A Nice wa niteru</b>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.890
<i>“Watch out” and “Have a nice” are similar</i>

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.650
<b>Soudochira mo kamihitoe na no sa</b>

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.650
<i>That’s right – both are by the skin of your teeth</i>

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:16.660
<b>Taikutsu nugisuteteima sugu kakedase</b>

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:16.660
<i>Throw boredom away and start running right now</i>

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.410
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:24.750
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.920
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:38.030
This is Seahawk. This is Seahawk.

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:39.370
Headquarters, come in.

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:42.450
Headquarters, come in. This is Seahawk.

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:46.290
This is the Intelligence Agency. Seahawk, come in.

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:48.330
The radio jamming is getting worse.

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:51.500
Transmission from the satellite is completely shut off.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.090
The radar is also not working!

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:54.300
What's going on?

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:57.550
Someone is obviously trying to sabotage us.

00:01:57.840 --> 00:01:59.390
It can't be.

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:00.930
What's that?

00:02:04.810 --> 00:02:06.310
Emergency alert!

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:09.940
This is Seahawk!

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:11.520
This is the Intelligence Agency.

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:21.700
Someone is sabotaging us!

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:24.790
Seahawk, what is your status?

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:28.460
It's a huge pirate ship! No, it's a galleon!

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:31.540
What are you talking about? Calm down and tell me what's happening!

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:38.880
What happened, Seahawk?

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:41.720
Seahawk!

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:44.890
Seahawk, come in!

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:46.850
Seahawk!

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:58.720
Episode 47

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:58.720
Decisive Battle on the Equator!!

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:03.120
Next, a disaster at sea.

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:10.460
The Maritime Research Foundation's research vessel Seahawk disappeared after leaving an SOS message.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:15.880
GUN is searching from the sky and from sea, but their whereabouts are still unknown.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:21.380
At the time of the incident, there was heavy fog at the Gran Pacific Sea.

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:26.260
The authorities believe there must have been an accident.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:28.270
The ocean really is scary.

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:31.440
That's because you don't like water, Sonic.

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:35.560
Maybe it crashed into something inside the fog.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:37.110
That's strange.

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:42.910
The accident took place at a location where there should be no fog.

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:44.240
But the news said-

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:46.280
That's the problem.

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:50.870
There are ugly rumors about the Maritime Research Foundation.

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:53.580
We should investigate.

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:56.040
Is scary things going to happen again?

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:58.210
Who knows.

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:02.550
You're thinking about Emerl again.

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:06.350
Don't mind! I'll never do anything to make you feel sad, Cream!

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:07.600
I promise!

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:10.310
Thank you, Sonic.

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:21.110
I have no idea what happened.

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:24.360
A pirate ship or galleon in this day and age?

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:28.330
Topaz must have gone insane right before the accident.

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:31.040
We don't know if it was an accident.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:37.210
Topaz did say that someone was sabotaging them.

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:40.340
Anyway, finding out where Seahawk went is more important.

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:42.170
You're right, Rouge.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:48.680
If it fell into enemy hands, our country's defense will be in danger.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:50.430
Our enemy?

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:52.060
It's just speculation.

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:58.860
Seahawk receives and analyzes information from our satellites.

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:01.360
This smells like an egg.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.070
Dr. Eggman.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:07.070
It's finally time for us to use that.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:10.240
Contact the GUN commander immediately!

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:15.410
This is a useful system.

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:20.750
Dr. Eggman, what are you using the latest system to look for?

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:25.630
Dr. Eggman, what are you looking for using the latest system?

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:29.220
Stop talking! You're so noisy!

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:32.850
Knuckles found the oldest map in the world.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:38.520
The archeology geophysicist Dr. Atsumi arrives at Pukapito Palace.

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:40.980
This is it!

00:05:56.330 --> 00:06:02.840
This old map will prove my theory is correct.

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:05.210
We found it.

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:08.970
Let's steal it and take it back to Dr. Eggman.

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:11.220
What?

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:12.640
Can't you tell that we're mummies?

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:15.390
We're not severely injured people.

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:19.900
It worked!

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:23.820
That went really well! Now let's flee!

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:33.030
It's them!

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:36.290
My favorite chive bun!

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:40.290
Stop, you punks!

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:44.090
Stop!

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:54.760
What am I feeling?

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:56.640
Our plan worked!

00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:59.640
Let's stay a bit longer.

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:07.230
You two are late.

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:11.990
Well, it's fine. Good job.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:33.220
<i>Note: "Bellybutton" in Japanese is "heso".</i>

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:32.090
I found it! This is the world's bellybutton!

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:33.220
Heh? So?

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:36.930
Stop with those lame old jokes.

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:37.810
An old guy is saying they're old?

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:39.930
It's showtime!

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:39.520
Yeah, right?

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:41.940
Just watch, everyone!

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:47.520
This time, mankind will kneel in fear of Dr. Eggman!

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:02.250
Hi, Knuckles.

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:04.000
Long time no see, Ella.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:06.380
And who's this gentleman?

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:08.710
I'm from the Pukapito Palace Museum.

00:08:08.710 --> 00:08:10.380
Dr. Atsumi!

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:14.550
Oh, you were in my class at Yamato University.

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:16.890
You remembered me, Doctor!

00:08:16.890 --> 00:08:20.270
I'm crying in gratitude and happiness!

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:22.940
So you're working here as their gardener?

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:28.150
No. I'm the Thorndyke family's butler and bodyguard.

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:34.450
You're as dependable as ever.

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:40.620
According to Knuckles, the two were Eggman's minions.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:43.290
Yeah, the usual stooges.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:47.500
Why did they want this map?

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:50.210
Have you heard of the continent of Murasia?

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:51.710
Continent of Murasia?

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:59.180
Long before the beginning of our civilization, there was the continent of Murasia.

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:03.430
The people who lived there were an advanced civilization.

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:07.400
But about twelve thousand years ago...

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:15.820
Due to a gigantic shift in the Earth's crust, it's said that the continent sank into the Gran Pacific Sea.

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:24.790
That means Eggman is after something that has to do with the continent of Murasia.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:29.000
It feels like there's a connection with the Seahawk incident.

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:33.170
I want to make the first move, but how?

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:43.810
Dr. Thorndyke, this map accurately depicts when all the land on this planet was connected as one.

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:48.810
When I add the land movement data...

00:09:56.200 --> 00:10:04.160
Do you see it? If you compare this map with the current land formation, there's one location that's missing.

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:07.460
Is it the continent of Murasia?

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:08.790
That's right.

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:16.300
With the data from this map, I have identified the location of the lost continent of Murasia.

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:19.470
It's in the Gran Pacific Sea at zero latitude.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:29.390
Be careful!

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:31.980
Take care!

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:34.150
See you later!

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:35.900
Behave yourselves!

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:37.690
Bye!

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:40.820
Come back soon!

00:10:57.710 --> 00:10:59.680
We'll arrive tomorrow.

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:03.180
There's only a dormant volcano here.

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:09.390
However, there's an underwater chain of volcanoes, so this is the most unstable area in the world.

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:12.230
I hope nothing bad happens.

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:14.820
Something always happens.

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:17.860
And the reason why you look so tense is-

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:20.610
Stop! I'm no longer afraid of the sea!

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:23.030
Probably.

00:11:27.740 --> 00:11:29.250
We're finally here.

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:32.000
Let's hurry up and search that island, guys.

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:33.920
You're full of energy.

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:35.250
The underwater radar has detected something!

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:38.170
A gigantic object is approaching the ship!

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:42.630
What's that?

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:58.150
The X-Cyclone!

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:31.730
That symbol is...

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:32.980
Eggman!

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:41.440
I have a message for you from Dr. Eggman!

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:45.070
Are you surprised?

00:12:45.070 --> 00:12:50.450
This is my latest weapon in building the Eggman Empire, the Egg Giant Makan!

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:53.000
Eggman, what are you after now?

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:55.120
Do you want me to tell you?

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:57.250
Fine, I'll tell you.

00:12:57.250 --> 00:13:00.000
We know you're dying to tell us.

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:03.380
Have you heard of the world's bellybutton?

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:04.800
World's bellybutton?

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:06.180
I have!

00:13:06.260 --> 00:13:08.510
It's an underground magma pressure point.

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:13.390
Stimulating it will cause all the volcanoes in the world to erupt.

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:17.810
It's one of Earth's oldest legends.

00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:21.070
Very good, Atsumi. You're so smart.

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:25.320
But I bet you didn't know that this spot was the world's bellybutton!

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:27.410
Ah, I see.

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:35.500
The Murasia people may have stimulated the world's bellybutton, causing the land to shift and their continent to sink.

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:37.370
Dr. Atsumi, that means...

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:45.590
My theory is that Murasia survivors spread around the world, creating new civilizations.

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:49.140
What's with the serious explanation?

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:51.970
This scene is supposed to be more intense!

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:56.180
"My theory is that..." This isn't the time for that!

00:13:56.440 --> 00:14:04.190
You have to be more nervous! I'm going to stimulate the world's bellybutton and destroy the world!

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:06.360
I won't let you do that!

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:12.030
Sonic!

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:13.740
Chris!

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:24.630
Sonic!

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:27.670
Chris!

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:32.890
Chris, pull yourself together!

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:39.310
Keep going!

00:14:37.270 --> 00:14:40.600
Dr. Eggman is missing on purpose and having fun.

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:46.650
Damn!

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:49.150
Hang on, Sonic!

00:14:51.740 --> 00:14:54.240
Chris! Sonic!

00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:55.990
Stop! It's too dangerous!

00:14:55.990 --> 00:14:56.870
But Doctor!

00:14:56.870 --> 00:14:59.080
Just wait, Tanaka!

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:02.330
Can't you do anything? They're in danger!

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:05.090
I know! I need a little more time.

00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:09.800
Sonic, don't you dare let go!

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:11.300
Never give up!

00:15:16.390 --> 00:15:18.890
There's a signal at Point 2090!

00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:21.230
I don't understand those numbers!

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:24.270
Something is approaching from portside stern!

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:26.230
It's enormous!

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:28.030
Is it a new enemy?

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:47.670
Are you surprised, Eggman?

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:52.180
This is GUN's ultimate weapon, the GUN Fort V3!

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:53.930
It's on our side!

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:55.260
It's GUN!

00:15:55.350 --> 00:16:01.310
What are you talking about? That's the Egg Fort 1 that I left at the bottom of the ocean!

00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:02.770
It's good that they recycle.

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:05.310
You fool! They did more than just copy us. They stole from us!

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:08.070
The underdog always barks before the fight.

00:16:08.070 --> 00:16:10.530
Windmill and Kurt, are you ready?

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:11.240
Roger!

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:13.110
What about me?

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:15.410
A guest should sit there and stay quiet.

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:17.330
Start the attack!

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:20.580
If you want to fight, then I accept your challenge!

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:22.540
Flight mode!

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:24.120
Yeah!

00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:41.020
Broadside cannons, fire!

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:47.150
Fire anti-missiles and ultimate depth charges!

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:53.400
I'm glad that you're safe.

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:55.860
I owe GUN one.

00:16:57.910 --> 00:16:59.030
They're coming this way!

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:01.450
Turn and return fire! Hard to starboard!

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:03.330
Which way is starboard?

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:04.120
It doesn't matter!

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:06.120
Just turn!

00:17:10.460 --> 00:17:13.720
Did you see what GUN Fort V3 can do?

00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:16.380
X-Cyclone, take off!

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:28.400
Change to X-Tornado!

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:41.240
They're attacking from both sides!

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:43.200
It's time for my ace in the hole!

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:52.420
Topaz! You're alive!

00:17:54.380 --> 00:18:00.470
What do you think will happen to them if you lay a finger on Egg Giant Makan?

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:02.720
That's not fair, Eggman!

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:05.350
I'm a villain. Of course I'm not fair.

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:07.440
If you don't like that, then attack me!

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:12.320
What are you doing?

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:13.860
Don't stop us, Rouge.

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:16.950
Our mission is to stop Eggman.

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:20.530
I'm sorry, but you'll have to forget about Topaz.

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:22.280
What are you talking about?

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:25.540
That's how it is.

00:18:31.590 --> 00:18:34.590
They're attacking? They're monsters!

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:37.920
You, of all people, have no right to say that.

00:18:38.050 --> 00:18:39.630
At this rate, they're going to be killed!

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:42.510
I know. Are you ready, Sonic?

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:44.140
Of course!

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:52.400
Sonic, you traitor!

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:57.570
Give me ten minutes.

00:18:57.820 --> 00:19:01.620
Fine, ten minutes. But we won't wait for a second longer.

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:05.700
They're fighting amongst themselves.

00:19:05.700 --> 00:19:09.040
Now's our chance to head towards the world's bellybutton!

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:14.590
It's the bat girl!

00:19:14.590 --> 00:19:16.460
She's planning to save her friends.

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:18.260
Eggman is going to spot her!

00:19:18.260 --> 00:19:19.720
Is she planning a diversion?

00:19:32.940 --> 00:19:36.520
That fly is annoying!

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:42.160
